00:55:53.150 --> 00:55:55.190
has trained using our own data.

00:55:55.190 --> 00:55:59.090
There's the Vision API to
extract insight from images.

00:55:59.090 --> 00:56:00.810
What's in the image?

00:56:00.810 --> 00:56:03.890
Recognize location, landmarks,
and a lot of things like that.

00:56:03.890 --> 00:56:09.160
Speech API to automatically
transcribe voice into text.

00:56:09.160 --> 00:56:11.630
Jobs API, that's a
pretty specialized API.

00:56:11.630 --> 00:56:14.630
But I think that that's
where the industry is going.

00:56:14.630 --> 00:56:16.970
In this case, having
an API specifically

00:56:16.970 --> 00:56:20.750
for matching candidates'
resumes to job opportunity.

00:56:20.750 --> 00:56:24.050
And something that goes way
beyond typical keyword matching

00:56:24.050 --> 00:56:27.590
and really has been trained on
really, really large amounts

00:56:27.590 --> 00:56:30.080
of data and has much
more insight about what

00:56:30.080 --> 00:56:35.180
actually makes
sense for matching.

